      self.final_answer_pattern = re.compile(r\"^final_answer\\((.*)\\)$\", re.M)\n50:         self.installed_packages = []\n```\n\nSubclasses in the same file:\n- `E2BExecutor` (line 96), `__init__` at lines 106–116: `def __init__(self, additional_imports: list[str], logger, **kwargs)` — passes `**kwargs` to `Sandbox(**kwargs)`.\n- `DockerExecutor` (line 160), `__init__` at lines 165–187: `def __init__(self, additional_imports: list[str], logger, host: str = \"127.0.0.1\", port: int = 8888, image_name: str = \"jupyter-kernel\", build_new_image: bool = True, container_run_kwargs: dict[str, Any] | None = None)` — calls `super().__init__(additional_imports, logger)`.\n\n## 3. CodeAgent and Executor Creation\n\n**File:** `/testbed/src/smolagents/agents.py`\n- Class definition: **line 1210**; import of executors at line 48.\n- `__init__`: **lines 1228–1268**\n- `create_python_executor`: **lines 1270–1285**\n\n```python\n1228:     def __init__(\n1229:         self,\n1230:         tools: list[Tool],\n1231:         model: Model,\n1232:         prompt_templates: PromptTemplates | None = None,\n1233:         grammar: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n1234:         additional_authorized_imports: list[str] | None = None,\n1235:         planning_interval: int | None = None,\n1236:         executor_type: str | None = \"local\",\n1237:         executor_kwargs: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n1238:         max_print_outputs_length: int | None = None,\n1239:         stream_outputs: bool = False,\n1240:         **kwargs,\n1241:     ):\n          ...\n1266:         self.executor_type = executor_type or \"local\"\n1267:         self.executor_kwargs = executor_kwargs or {}\n1268:         self.python_executor = self.create_python_executor()\n\n1270:     def create_python_executor(self) -> PythonExecutor:\n1271:         match self.executor_type:\n1272:             case \"e2b\" | \"docker\":\n1273:                 if self.managed_agents:\n1274:                     raise Exception(\"Managed agents are not yet supported with remote code execution.\")\n1275:                 if self.executor_type == \"e2b\":\n1276:                     return E2BExecutor(self.additional_authorized_imports, self.logger, **self.executor_kwargs)\n1277:                 else:\n1278:                     return DockerExecutor(self.additional_authorized_imports, self.logger, **self.executor_kwargs)\n1279:             case \"local\":\n1280:                 return LocalPythonExecutor(\n1281:                     self.additional_authorized_imports,\n1282:                     max_print_outputs_length=self.max_print_outputs_length,\n1283:                 )\n1284:             case _:  # if applicable\n1285:                 raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported executor type: {self.executor_type}\")\n```\n\n**Key observation:** `executor_kwargs` is passed to `E2BExecutor`/`DockerExecutor` via `**self.executor_kwargs` (lines 1276, 1278), but it is **NOT** passed to `LocalPythonExecutor` (lines 1280–1283) — the local branch only passes `additional_authorized_imports` and `max_print_outputs_length`.\n\nSerialization usage in `CodeAgent.to_dict` (line 1424) and `CodeAgent.from_dict` (line 1443):\n```python\n1424:         agent_dict[\"executor_kwargs\"] = self.executor_kwargs\n...\n1443:             \"executor_kwargs\": agent_dict.get(\"executor_kwargs\"),\n```\n\nExecutor tool-wiring happens in `MultiStepAgent.run` (agents.py lines 343–345):\n```python\n343:         if getattr(self, \"python_executor\", None):\n344:             self.python_executor.send_variables(variables=self.state)\n345:             self.python_executor.send_tools({**self.tools, **self.managed_agents})\n```\n\n## 4. All Usages of `executor_kwargs`\n\n**`/testbed/src/smolagents/agents.py`** — lines 1222 (docstring), 1237 (param), 1267 (stored), 1276 & 1278 (passed to remote executors), 1424 (to_dict), 1443 (from_dict). *(Details above.)*\n\n**`/testbed/tests/test_agents.py`** — 7 occurrences:\n- Line 1233: `assert agent.executor_kwargs == {}` (in `test_from_folder`)\n- Line 1264: `\"executor_kwargs\": {\"max_workers\": 2},` (in `test_from_dict` agent_dict)\n- Line 1277: `assert agent.executor_kwargs == {\"max_workers\": 2}`\n- Line 1295: `CodeAgent.from_dict(agent_dict, additional_authorized_imports=[\"matplotlib\"], executor_kwargs={\"max_workers\": 4})`\n- Line 1298: `assert agent.executor_kwargs == {\"max_workers\": 4}`\n- Line 1320: `executor_kwargs={\"max_workers\": 2},` (in `test_multiagents_save` CodeAgent construction)\n- Line 1359: `assert agent2.executor_kwargs == {\"max_workers\": 2}` (after `from_folder` reload)\n\n**`/testbed/tests/fixtures/agents.py`** — line 45 (comment) and line 86: `\"executor_kwargs\": {},` in the \"v1.10\" agent dict fixture.\n\n## 5. Tests Related to Executor Initialization\n\n**`/testbed/tests/test_agents.py`:**\n- `test_local_python_executor_with_custom_functions` (**lines 1203–1210**) — the only place `additional_functions` appears in tests; it sets the attribute directly after construction rather than passing it to `__init__`:\n```python\n1203:     def test_local_python_executor_with_custom_functions(self):\n1204:         model = MagicMock()\n1205:         model.last_input_token_count = 10\n1206:         model.last_output_token_count = 5\n1207:         agent = CodeAgent(tools=[], model=model)\n1208:         agent.python_executor.additional_functions = {\"open\": open}\n1209:         agent.run(\"Test run\")\n1210:         assert \"open\" in agent.python_executor.static_tools\n```\n- `test_from_folder` (lines 1212–1241), `test_from_dict` (lines 1243–1298), `test_multiagents_save` (lines 1302–1363) — all assert `executor_kwargs` round-tripping through save/from_dict/from_folder.\n\n**`/testbed/tests/test_local_python_executor.py`:**\n- `TestLocalPythonExecutor` class (line 1684): `test_state_name` (1685–1687), `test_call_from_dict` (1696–1699), `test_chained_assignments` (1727–1731), `test_evaluate_assign_error` (1733–1737). All instantiate `LocalPythonExecutor([])` or `LocalPythonExecutor(additional_authorized_imports=[])` — **none pass `additional_functions` to the constructor**.\n- `TestLocalPythonExecutorSecurity` class (line 1740): many tests instantiate with `additional_authorized_imports` only (lines 1746, 1759, 1772, 1791, 1812, 1829, 1846, 1867, 1884, 1961, 1984, 2023, 2071, 2107, 2128, 2155, 2160).\n- Line 1102–1104: standalone executor usage with `executor.send_tools({\"final_answer\": FinalAnswerTool()})`.\n\n**`/testbed/tests/test_remote_executors.py`:**\n- `TestRemotePythonExecutor` (lines 18–34): instantiates `RemotePythonExecutor(additional_imports=[], logger=MagicMock())` (lines 20, 30) and tests `send_tools`.\n- `TestE2BExecutorMock.test_e2b_executor_instantiation` (lines 37–45): `E2BExecutor(additional_imports=[], logger=logger, api_key=\"dummy-api-key\", template=\"dummy-template-id\", timeout=60)` — demonstrates remote executors accepting extra kwargs.\n\n**`/testbed/tests/test_cli.py`:** line 6 imports `LocalPythonExecutor`; line 109 calls `LocalPythonExecutor([\"helium\"])(\"from helium import *\")`.\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Key Findings\n\n1. `LocalPythonExecutor.__init__` accepts `(additional_authorized_imports, max_print_outputs_length=None, additional_functions=None)` — the `additional_functions` parameter exists but `CodeAgent.create_python_executor` never passes it.\n2. `RemotePythonExecutor.__init__` accepts only `(additional_imports, logger)`; its subclasses (`E2BExecutor`, `DockerExecutor`) additionally accept `**kwargs` / named params, which is where `CodeAgent` forwards `**self.executor_kwargs`.\n3. `CodeAgent.create_python_executor` (agents.py line 1270) currently **ignores `self.executor_kwargs` for the `\"local\"` executor type** — only `e2b`/`docker` branches forward it.\n4. `additional_functions` is consumed in `LocalPythonExecutor.send_tools` (line 1545), merged into `static_tools` alongside agent tools and `BASE_PYTHON_TOOLS`.\n5. Existing tests never pass `additional_functions` through the constructor; one test (`test_local_python_executor_with_custom_functions`, test_agents.py:1203) monkey-patches the attribute post-construction.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f96fae886ffeTAL3nDa6Kuwc9a","sessionId":"ses_f96fac77bffeB5Zg0XWWswwf0K","model":{"modelID":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","providerID":"openrouter"},"truncated":false},"title":"Find executor and CodeAgent code","time":{"start":1788468344969,"end":1788468423341}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me explore the codebase to understand the structure and find the relevant files for LocalPythonExecutor, RemotePythonExecutor, and CodeAgent.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_06905387b0013PSlwTD7zZqV3u","sessionID":"ses_f96fae886ffeTAL3nDa6Kuwc9a","messageID":"msg_0690519720015oueBtChlivGYG"}}
