{"type":"text","timestamp":1788468622594,"sessionID":"ses_f96fae886ffeTAL3nDa6Kuwc9a","part":{"id":"prt_069096654001H1ni5eSVsbj4Aw","messageID":"msg_0690959360012xTb9DAtgPH0qG","sessionID":"ses_f96fae886ffeTAL3nDa6Kuwc9a","type":"text","text":"Done. `executor_kwargs` is now forwarded to `LocalPythonExecutor`, matching upstream PR #1314:\n\n**Change** — src/smolagents/agents.py:1279: `CodeAgent.create_python_executor` now merges `executor_kwargs` into the `LocalPythonExecutor` init call, using dict-merge so `executor_kwargs` can even override `max_print_outputs_length`:\n\n```python\ncase \"local\":\n    return LocalPythonExecutor(\n        self.additional_authorized_imports,\n        **{\"max_print_outputs_length\": self.max_print_outputs_length} | self.executor_kwargs,\n    )\n```\n\n**Tests updated** (tests/test_agents.py): `max_workers` values (only ever used as inert serialization payloads) replaced with valid local-executor kwargs, and `test_local_python_executor_with_custom_functions` now passes `additional_functions` via `executor_kwargs` instead of patching the attribute post-creation.\n\n**Verified**: all 6 executor-related agent tests pass, plus functional checks — `executor_kwargs={\"additional_functions\": {...}}` lands in `static_tools`, overrides of `max_print_outputs_length` apply, and agents without `executor_kwargs` behave exactly as before. The 2 scipy/sklearn test failures are pre-existing environment issues unrelated to this change.","time":{"start":1788468618836,"end":1788468622590}}}
